  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "Two of three columns centre coherently on one inferable focus -- the recurring problem-type taxonomy -- with problem_type providing a granular inferred category and is_connectivity_issue providing a sensible higher-level grouping facet. This is clearly not a scattered grab-bag, and the focus is highly actionable (an analyst can rank, cluster, and prioritise recurring problem classes). Structure quality is dragged down because the set is thin: is_connectivity_issue is largely a derivative restatement of problem_type rather than an orthogonal facet, and resolution_days is completely NULL and off-focus (it addresses resolution time, not problem type), adding no analytical value. A stronger structure would have added orthogonal facets of the problem taxonomy (e.g., affected system/service, root-cause class, severity pattern) rather than a duplicate boolean and an empty column."
}
